  "grammar": {
    "exact": "UTF-8 string equality after NFC normalization; the characters *, ?, [, and ] are forbidden",
    "prefix": "UTF-8 byte-prefix comparison after NFC normalization; prefix values contain no wildcard metacharacters and match only values beginning with the complete literal prefix",
    "providerPermission": "provider, permissionKey, and level are exact values; resourcesExact uses exact grammar and optional resourcesPrefix uses prefix grammar",
    "applicationAuthorization": "An authorization row is an AND of all selectorsExact and all required prefix categories; rows for the same action are OR alternatives and exactly one row must match. A category is the nonempty text before the first colon. Every category is required exactly once; multiple declared prefixes within a category are OR alternatives, not optional selectors. Exact and prefix categories may not overlap.",
    "comparison": "Effective provider permissions equal providerPermissions. Selectors are a closed set: the supplied category set must exactly equal requiredSelectorCategories, with one value per category. Every selectorsExact value must be present and equal after NFC normalization. Each prefix category must have exactly one supplied value matching one listed literal prefix. Missing, duplicate (including same category with different values), malformed, wildcard, unknown, extra or wrong selectors deny. Zero or multiple matching authorization rows deny. Every provider permission maps via applicationActionsExact to existing named application actions; absent, empty or unrecognized mappings fail. Extra permission, action, audience, lifetime or delegation fails.",
    "selectorAuthority": "Request selectors are materialized from independently verified authentication, tenant/repository context and current authorization-policy evaluation, not caller assertions. organization must match the authenticated organization. active-hat:required is emitted only when the verified subject currently has the action-required eligible hat for this exact item; absence, ineligibility, or caller-only assertion denies. authorization-state selectors require current named authorization records.",
    "requiredSelectorCategories": "For each row this exact set equals the union of categories in selectorsExact and selectorsPrefix. All are required, none optional. Every row includes organization. selectorsExact categories are unique; prefix alternatives may share a category, but may not overlap an exact category.",
    "providerActionMapping": "applicationActionsExact is the exhaustive permitted-purpose mapping in both directions. Every provider permission maps to one or more existing exact provider-backed application actions. Every application action with providerAccess=required is named by at least one declared provider permission. An action may avoid that reverse requirement only when providerAccess=internal-only, its action begins internal:, it has a nonempty internalOnlyReasonExact, and no provider permission maps to it. Missing, extra, orphan, unknown, contradictory or reclassified mappings fail."
  },
